        <section id="so-what-is-testing?"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          So what is testing?
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Testing can be defined as the process of evaluating software, a system, or its components with the intent to find out whether it satisfies the specified requirements or not.</p>
<p>To ensure that each piece of code works the way it is supposed to there are a number of different types, level, and methods of testing carried out.</p>
<p>Most testing methods can be categorised as either functional or non-functional which you will learn more about on this page. You will also learn about how testing is a critical element within software development cycle.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/cp3/cp3_u4_s1_p2_image.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
